v/provider config is passed through ao spawn; whether AO's usage endpoint and the gateway both report tokens and cost; the key's max budget and current spend; list prices for all seven models with sources.\n   b. Any of S1, S3, S4, S5 and the fly-doom-jev test check not yet finished. Skip S6 unless `claude mcp list` shows cfoai connected.\n   c. Then lane A proper: the run loop, ledger writer, dry-run mode with simulated workers (`tally demo` and `tally run --dry-run`), then the adapters (AO spawn/status/kill + usage polling, GitHub issues intake, Entire, neatlogs, cfo.ai with the CSV fallback). Lane B owns agent/ and will define the ports it needs from you in agent/ports.ts; lane C owns dashboard/ and demo/. Stay out of those folders.\n\nOpen one PR per coherent piece rather than one giant PR. Report with `ao report` at each milestone."}]},"uuid":"1f9f0ad4-4923-40e7-a341-4bfd974f86ee","timestamp":"2026-10-10T11:43:17.786Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":3,"turnIndex":3},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-2","sessionId":"01cec7b7-211c-4580-a570-667a1d97cc45","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"ao/neatlogs-hack-2/root"}
