556	// ensureWorkspaceTrusted records workspacePath as trusted in Claude Code's
557	// config so the interactive trust dialog does not block a spawned session.
558	//
559	// It is additive and concurrency-safe: it reads the existing config, sets
560	// only projects[workspacePath].hasTrustDialogAccepted = true (preserving the
561	// rest of the entry and every other project), and writes back via a
562	// temp-file + atomic rename. If the path is already trusted, it makes no
563	// write at all. A missing config file is treated as an empty one; a
564	// zero-byte or corrupt config file is refused rather than overwritten.
565	// claudeTrustMu serializes ensureWorkspaceTrusted within the process. Concurrent
566	// spawns to different workspaces otherwise read the same ~/.claude.json snapshot
567	// and the last rename drops the other's trust entry.
568	var claudeTrustMu sync.Mutex
